rogeneity on the high seas</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><year>2004</year><volume>378</volume><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>292</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14662007</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1042/BJ20031672</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ikonen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Roles of lipid rafts in membrane transport</article-title><source>Curr Opin Cell Biol</source><year>2001</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>470</fpage><lpage>477</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11454454</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0955-0674(00)00238-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Varma</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayor</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GPI-anchored proteins are organized in submicron domains at the cell surface</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1998</year><volume>394</volume><fpage>798</fpage><lpage>801</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9723621</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/29563</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vey</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pilkuhn</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wille</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nixon</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>DeArmond</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Smart</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Taraboulos</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Prusiner</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sub